# GitHub Workflows

This plugin provides three skills for common GitHub operations. Load the
relevant skill for the requested task.

## create-issue

Identify the target repository and collect the issue title, body, labels, and
assignees from the request and conversation. Follow repository contribution
guidelines and issue templates retrieved from the GitHub API. Draft when asked
for advice; create the issue when creation is authorized.

## create-pull-request

Identify the target repository, base, and head. Inspect the complete
base-to-head commit log and diff to understand the change and write an accurate
title and description. Include relevant verification and disclose checks not
run.

Retrieve contribution guidelines and PR templates from the target repository's
GitHub API. Select the applicable template; if multiple choices are plausible
and intent does not resolve the choice, ask the user. Follow its structure and
applicable repository instructions without inventing facts.

Draft when asked for a draft or advice; create the PR when creation is
authorized. Do not split the PR or rename the branch as part of this workflow.

## merge-pull-request

Identify the target repository and PR. Check the merge requirements (CI status,
required reviews, branch protection) before merging. Use the merge method
specified by the user or the repository default. Report the outcome.
